From 414e3eec2eb1abb947dd4a1c5525ddf2676766af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:11:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bdj: warm up the graphics pipeline once per JVM

Discs time the player's graphics speed when their menu starts and fall back
to a simpler menu below a threshold. Superman UHD fills and blits a 720x480
image 100 times and wants >= 85 per second for its sliding menu; on the
first disc after the JVM starts the span/blend loops are still interpreted
and it scores ~63 (a minute later ~101 on the same box), so the first play
never slides. Standalone players are never cold.

At the end of the first Libbluray.init(), run the same kind of work on
private offscreen images in a low-priority daemon thread (<= 300 rounds or
1.5 s) so the JIT compiles those loops first. Nothing is drawn to screen.
---
 .../bdj/java/java/awt/BDGraphicsWarmup.java   | 114 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../bdj/java/org/videolan/Libbluray.java      |   7 ++
 2 files changed, 121 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/libbluray/bdj/java/java/awt/BDGraphicsWarmup.java

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/java/awt/BDGraphicsWarmup.java b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/java/awt/BDGraphicsWarmup.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ced6317
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/java/awt/BDGraphicsWarmup.java
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
